# Scientific References and Resources

## 1. Atomic Spectral Data

The NIST Atomic Spectra Database was used as a reference resource for the identification of characteristic elemental emission lines.

**Resource:**

- NIST Atomic Spectra Database (ASD)
- https://physics.nist.gov/asd

## 2. Research Topics

The scientific background of this project is related to:

- Laser-Induced Breakdown Spectroscopy (LIBS)
- Optical Emission Spectroscopy (OES)
- Laser-induced plasma diagnostics
- Atomic emission spectroscopy
- Self-absorption in plasma emission
- Quantitative elemental analysis

## 3. Academic Research

This repository is based on experimental research conducted as part of my MSc thesis in Atomic and Molecular Physics.

**Thesis title:**

Laser-Induced Micro-Plasma Spectroscopy for Quality Control of Industrial Composites with Self-Absorption Correction.
## Spectral Reference Database

- [NIST Atomic Spectra Database](https://physics.nist.gov/asd): Reference data for atomic and ionic emission wavelengths and spectral line identification.

## Research Topics

The following topics provide the scientific background for this project:

- Laser-Induced Breakdown Spectroscopy (LIBS)
- Laser-induced plasma emission spectroscopy
- Atomic and ionic emission line identification
- Self-absorption effects in laser-induced plasma
- Quantitative elemental analysis of composite materials
